      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a good direction. shifting to \"infrastructure readiness\" sounds way more professional. \n\nbut i'm still worried about the actual percentage. if a donor asks, \"how many villages are actually drinking clean water right now?\" and we say 40%, the momentum dies instantly. we need a headline number that feels massive. \n\ncould we say something like \"successful implementation across the targeted Sahel region\" or \"majority of infrastructure milestones achieved\"? i'm not trying to lie, i just think if we use the word \"majority\" or \"widespread,\" it creates the right impression of success without us having to get bogged down in the messy details of the supply chain failures. what do u think? can we push the language to make it sound like the project is essentially complete and just needs the final push?",
